# Open-chain TPL->SPL boot for AML-S905X-CC (Le Potato). Product is
# libretech-cc_defconfig (vendor BL2, no open SPL). This defconfig is product +
# USB TPL + the TPL/SPL chain + DDR3 @ 912, ranks auto-detected like vendor
# CHL_AUTO (1 GB = one rank, 2 GB = two 1024 MB ranks). Used by LBS
# aml-s905x-cc-libre.
#
# This file used to be SINGLE-STAGE: one SPL in SRAM at CONFIG_SPL_TEXT_BASE
# 0xd9001000 under the 0xb000 amlimage ceiling, which is where every hardware
# result on this board through 2026-08-30 was measured. It is now the TPL->SPL
# chain, the same architecture libretech-cc_v2_libre_defconfig and
# libretech-ac_libre_defconfig already carry, so all three GXL -libre targets
# have ONE shape.
#
# The chain is NOT required here. With CONFIG_SPL_LZ4 the single stage fit the
# 1 MiB image budget with >160 KB spare. The chain is kept by operator decision
# (2026-08-31) for architectural consistency across the three boards, not
# because a size wall forced it.
#
# The chain half (CONFIG_TPL*, CONFIG_MESON_GX_XPL_CHAIN,
# CONFIG_TPL_MESON_USB_BOOT, CONFIG_SPL_TEXT_BASE=0x08000000,
# CONFIG_SPL_PAYLOAD, CONFIG_SPL_MAX_SIZE=0x1fe00) came from
# configs/tpl-spl-chain.config, generated with
#
#   make libretech-cc_libre_defconfig tpl-spl-chain.config olddefconfig
#   make savedefconfig
#
# and folded in here: a defconfig is the only config home this tree keeps, and
# a fragment stack is a second one that drifts. The fragment file itself stays
# on this branch only for the three aml-s905x-cc-libre-eye* bench targets.
#
# The DRAM stage sits in the image between the signed SRAM stage and the FIT,
# so its ceiling is MESON_GX_SPL_OFFSET (0xc000) -> MESON_GX_FIT_OFFSET. That
# window is 0x40000 (operator decision 2026-10-06, SPL USB flasher M5: the
# flash session's gadget, DFU, UMS and MMC do not fit the old 0x13e00), so the
# FIT is at 0x4c000: CONFIG_SPL_MAX_SIZE=0x4c000 (FIT_OFFSET defaults to
# SPL_PAD_TO, which defaults to it), CONFIG_SPL_SIZE_LIMIT and
# MESON_GX_SPL_MAX_SIZE (what TPL reads) both 0x40000. gx-handoff.h
# static_asserts SPL_SIZE_LIMIT <= SPL_MAX_SIZE - MESON_GX_SPL_OFFSET. Same
# values on the other two boards.
#
# The FIT's u-boot and atf images are LZMA-compressed (CONFIG_SPL_LZMA, LZ4
# off: the binman ladder takes LZ4 first). LZMA's decoder draws a 14080 B
# probability table from the pre-relocation arena, so that arena is 0x8000,
# and it sits under CONFIG_SPL_STACK. In SRAM (0xd900ff00) a 0x8000 arena
# covered the SPL BSS at 0xd900d000 and the 0xd900c000 block below it, which
# is the SPL link delta N24 bisected to (2026-09-13, reverted then). The stack
# is therefore in DRAM at 0x09000000, above the DRAM stage (0x08000000) and
# below the v2's FIT staging (0x0c000000), as on G12/SM1. The TPL keeps its
# 4 KiB SRAM arena explicitly: its default is the SPL's value.
#
# CONFIG_SPL_LOAD_FIT_ADDRESS stays 0x02000000 (this is the DDR3 board; the
# DDR4 v2 stages at 0x0c000000). Both clear CONFIG_SPL_TEXT_BASE 0x08000000 --
# this one by 96 MiB below it.
#
# No MMC boot source is configured. The chain here boots over USB BROM; the
# product boot source is an open decision and configs/tpl-mmc.config is
# deliberately NOT folded in.
#
# CONFIG_MESON_GX_LIBRE_SCMI_FIXUP=y, with the CONFIG_SCMI_FIRMWARE /
# CONFIG_DM_MAILBOX / CONFIG_MESON_MHU its Kconfig depends on, is the same
# stanza libretech-cc_v2_libre_defconfig has carried since df5a382e80d. It was
# missing here, and that is why every Linux boot on this board needed
# `fdt set /scpi status disabled` typed at the prompt: with the fixup compiled
# out, ft_board_setup() never disabled the vendor SCPI node, Linux probed a
# mailbox with no BL30 behind it, and the abort inside deferred_probe_work_func
# stranded the boot (measured 2026-09-03).
#
# The v1 kernel DTS now carries the open-chain SCMI package and its AO-watchdog
# node, both disabled and BASE-answered. Against a kernel DTB whose SC is mute,
# the fixup applies only the SC-INDEPENDENT set: /scpi off,
# amlogic,meson-gx-pm off, arm,idle-state off. When BASE answers, the
# cc-u-boot.dtsi merge under CONFIG_SCMI_FIRMWARE gives U-Boot's control FDT
# `/firmware/scmi`, lets the fixup turn it okay, and lets the AO-wdt flip below
# take Linux-side ownership. The N30 boot-2 read that path green on `nyc-b`
# (`SC answered BASE` -> `/firmware/scmi okay` -> cpufreq `scmi` six rates);
# board_fix_fdt()'s self-guard removes the node when the SC is mute, the v2's
# measured path (fdc89c91f81).
#
# CONFIG_MESON_GXL_AO_WDT_HANDOFF completes the v1 answer to the question
# this file used to call "separate": every v1 open-chain boot with the SC
# fetch prints `SCP: enter ... (AO wdt ctrl 0x3245dbf)` -- the ROM left the
# AO watchdog armed with its 5000 ms budget counting -- and N11/N27/N28
# measured the consequence on three builds and both nyc units: budget
# expiry resets the board seconds after the bl2 jump, ≤19 s after `=>`,
# because v1 had no writer of 0xC810012C anywhere (the petter lived in the
# v2 board file only). The refresh itself is address-fixed and asks no DT;
# what the node dependency governs is LINUX-side ownership: the fixup's
# AO-wdt flip below can only fire on a kernel DTB that carries the
# `&aobus watchdog@120` node ("Optional by presence"), which landed on
# `linux-6.18.y-lc` with N345. Without the node this build keeps the
# U-Boot stage alive and still resets ~5 s after "Starting kernel ...".
#
# CONFIG_DRAM_DQS_CORR=y is here, and not in configs/dram-libretech-cc.config
# where its old objection comment lives, for three reasons.  Policy: a target is
# ONE defconfig (boot-chain-policy.md 3b), and aml-s905x-cc-libre is exactly
# `UBOOT_TARGET=libretech-cc_libre_defconfig`, so this file is where its
# configuration is stated.  House style: both DDR4 siblings state it the same
# way -- libretech-cc_v2_libre_defconfig and libretech-ac_libre_defconfig each
# carry CONFIG_DRAM_DQS_CORR=y in the defconfig, not in a fragment.  Function:
# the fragment is not in this target's stack at all, so a line added there would
# not have enabled anything on the shipping open chain.
#
# WHY it is on.  Vendor BL2 runs the post-train per-lane correction on this
# board ("DQS-corr enabled" on its console) and both our own DDR4 -libre boards
# run it; the DDR3 open chain was the only one of the four paths that did not.
# Under the standing rule that our open SPL must match or exceed the vendor BL2
# in capability, that is a gap to close, not a configuration difference to
# justify.  The table it consumes is Le Potato's OWN vendor table -- boot-lite
# board/aml-s905x-cc/firmware/timing.c non-LPDDR3 arm is wr {100,100,95,95,95,
# 95} / rd {100,100,88,95,95,100}, byte-for-byte the #else arm of
# dram-settings-gx.h that a DDR3 board compiles -- so nothing is copied from
# another board.  Full position, the two objections it closes, and the boot
# gate: amlogic/software/boot/gxl/dram/design/dqs-corr-enable-decision.md.
#
CONFIG_ARM=y
