# G5/D3 pairing ACTIVE (was the N54 landing interim 0x0, u-boot be165435a3d):
# N340's cells are sourced (scp-firmware boards/aml-s905x-cc.c, N30 round --
# every rail/OPP/wake cell from this board's own V1.1-A/V1.0 sheets) and the
# v1-built contract bin carries trailer 0xb0a40101, so this board now NAMES
# its payload: spl-gxl-scp.c compares the staged trailer word against this id
# BEFORE the 0xd3 fetch and refuses a foreign one by name (the interim existed
# while the only bootable v1 payload was the cc-v2-described bin; N27 measured
# what the zero-cell v1 bin compiled to, and N28/N29 priced the interim's
# DVFS-pin hazard on the shipped one). Registry: gxl_board.h; the host-side
# twin of this claim is the board-id gate in the docs tree.
CONFIG_MESON_GXL_SCP_BOARD_ID=0x1
CONFIG_MESON_GX_LIBRE_SCMI_FIXUP=y
CONFIG_MESON_GXL_AO_WDT_HANDOFF=y
CONFIG_SPL_SYS_MALLOC_F_LEN=0x8000
CONFIG_DRAM_TWO_IDENTICAL_RANKS=y
# VDDEE 1000 mV on PWM_B, the same word as AML-S905X-CC-V2: the V1.1-A sheet's
# VDDEE divider is V2's (1R22 100K / 1R23 120K / 1R35 1M + 1R1 100K from
# GPIODV_29), so 0x000e000e is 1005 mV here too; left unprogrammed, GPIODV_29
# is undriven and 1R6 (10K to VDD_EE) sets about 1.06-1.16 V. Copper check:
# tools/pcb_power_path.py in the docs tree.
CONFIG_MESON_GXL_VDDEE_PWM_B=0xe000e
CONFIG_DRAM_DQS_CORR=y
CONFIG_DRAM_2T_MODE=y
